      "content": "#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <math.h>\n#include <omp.h>\n\n#define N_ITER 10\n#define DT 0.01f\n#define SOFTENING 1e-9f\n\ntypedef struct { float x, y, z, vx, vy, vz; } Body;\n\nstatic void body_force(float * restrict x, float * restrict y, float * restrict z,\n                       float * restrict vx, float * restrict vy, float * restrict vz,\n                       int n) {\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        float xi = x[i];\n        float yi = y[i];\n        float zi = z[i];\n        float fx = 0.0f, fy = 0.0f, fz = 0.0f;\n\n        #pragma omp simd reduction(+:fx,fy,fz) aligned(x,y,z:16)\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            float dx = x[j] - xi;\n            float dy = y[j] - yi;\n            float dz = z[j] - zi;\n            float sqrd_dist = dx*dx + dy*dy + dz*dz + SOFTENING;\n            float inv_dist = 1.0f / sqrt(sqrd_dist);\n            float inv_dist3 = inv_dist * inv_dist * inv_dist;\n\n            fx += dx * inv_dist3;\n            fy += dy * inv_dist3;\n            fz += dz * inv_dist3;\n        }\n\n        vx[i] += DT * fx;\n        vy[i] += DT * fy;\n        vz[i] += DT * fz;\n    }\n}\n\nstatic void read_soa(float **x, float **y, float **z,\n                     float **vx, float **vy, float **vz,\n                     int *nbodies) {\n    int b = fread(nbodies, sizeof(*nbodies), 1, stdin);\n    if (b != 1) { fprintf(stderr,\"Error reading nbodie value\\n\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n\n    size_t align = 16;\n    size_t sz = (*nbodies) * sizeof(float);\n\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)x, align, sz) != 0) exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)y, align, sz) != 0) exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)z, align, sz) != 0) exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)vx, align, sz) != 0) exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)vy, align, sz) != 0) exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    if (posix_memalign((void**)vz, align, sz) != 0) exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n\n    Body *tmp = (Body*)malloc(*nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n    b = fread(tmp, *nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdin);\n    if (b != 1) { fprintf(stderr,\"Error reading input values\\n\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < *nbodies; ++i) {\n        (*x)[i] = tmp[i].x;\n        (*y)[i] = tmp[i].y;\n        (*z)[i] = tmp[i].z;\n        (*vx)[i] = tmp[i].vx;\n        (*vy)[i] = tmp[i].vy;\n        (*vz)[i] = tmp[i].vz;\n    }\n\n    free(tmp);\n}\n\nstatic void write_soa(const int nbodies,\n                      float * restrict x, float * restrict y, float * restrict z,\n                      float * restrict vx, float * restrict vy, float * restrict vz) {\n    Body *tmp = (Body*)malloc(nbodies * sizeof(Body));\n    for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n        tmp[i].x = x[i];\n        tmp[i].y = y[i];\n        tmp[i].z = z[i];\n        tmp[i].vx = vx[i];\n        tmp[i].vy = vy[i];\n        tmp[i].vz = vz[i];\n    }\n    int b = fwrite(tmp, nbodies * sizeof(Body), 1, stdout);\n    if (b != 1) { fprintf(stderr,\"Error writing to output\\n\"); exit(EXIT_FAILURE); }\n    free(tmp);\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    float *x, *y, *z, *vx, *vy, *vz;\n    int nbodies;\n\n    read_soa(&x, &y, &z, &vx, &vy, &vz, &nbodies);\n\n    for (int iter = 0; iter < N_ITER; ++iter) {\n        body_force(x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, nbodies);\n\n        #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n        for (int i = 0; i < nbodies; ++i) {\n            x[i] += vx[i] * DT;\n            y[i] += vy[i] * DT;\n            z[i] += vz[i] * DT;\n        }\n    }\n\n    write_soa(nbodies, x, y, z, vx, vy, vz);\n\n    free(x); free(y); free(z); free(vx); free(vy); free(vz);\n    return EXIT_SUCCESS;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/nbody.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Converting from Array-of-Structs (AoS) to Struct-of-Arrays (SoA) layout with aligned allocation enables contiguous memory access for SIMD vectorization. Adding restrict qualifiers on pointers, hoisting outer loop coordinates into local variables, applying #pragma omp simd reduction on the inner force accumulation loop, and using OpenMP parallel for schedule(static) on both the outer force loop and position update loop allows efficient auto-vectorization with NEON instructions while maintaining thread-level parallelism. This combination should lower execution time below previous best results.",
  "notes": "Attempt to beat best known score of 0.7696 by combining SoA, alignment, restrict, SIMD reduction and OpenMP parallelism.",
